    "summary": "Rare Cryptical>China segues, solid set, but hissy tape",
    "blurb": "The Halloween show delivers a one‑off Cryptical Envelopment → China Cat Sunflower transition and strong energy on tracks like Dire Wolf and Easy Wind. Both soundboard sources are plagued by noticeable hiss and muffled fidelity, limiting the listening experience.",
    "review": "On October 31 1969 the Grateful Dead took the stage at San Jose State College for a Halloween set that has become a collector’s curiosity. The first half of the show is anchored by an unusual Cryptical Envelopment → China Cat Sunflower segue that never resurfaced elsewhere, followed by a classic I Know You Rider finish. Jerry Garcia’s vocals (notably his “cuz I'm hunting on top of the world” line) and overall playing were praised, and the band kept the momentum with solid renditions of Dire Wolf, Easy Wind, and a rousing Turn On Your Lovelight. However, both available soundboard recordings suffer from heavy hiss, muffled instruments, and a generally low‑fidelity capture that demands tape cleaning or restoration to be truly enjoyable.\n\nFor those willing to brave the audio flaws, the first recording (gd69-10-31.sbd.lai.3377.sbefail.shnf) is the most complete and captures the rare segue despite its poor quality. The second source (gd1969-10-31.131863.sbd-restore.droncit.flac16) offers a slightly clearer, though still cloudy, listening experience with stronger overall vibe. Fans should approach this show as a historical artifact rather than a pristine audio document.",
